6. Transitive dependencies
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Depending on the target framework and the consuming project's dependency graph,
the following transitive packages may be resolved at build time. NCMapper does
not redistribute any of them; they are listed so that the full picture is
available from one place.

  Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection  — MIT (net8.0/net9.0 stable, net10.0 preview)
  Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration         — MIT (test-only surface)
  SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlite3             — Apache-2.0  (see the CVE note below)
  Microsoft.Data.Sqlite                     — MIT         (ORM integration tests)

  CVE-2025-6965 note: EF Core Sqlite / Microsoft.Data.Sqlite transitively pin
  SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlite3 2.1.10, which bundles a SQLite build older than
  3.50.2 and is affected by CVE-2025-6965. NCMapper pins the bundle explicitly to
  2.1.13 (last of the 2.x line, bundling SQLite 3.53.x) so that consumers of the
  ORM integration packages are not exposed transitively. Upstream's constraint is
  a lower bound, so the explicit reference resolves without conflict.


